      "description": "As the German constitutional court delays its ruling on Article 26a, other member states begin unilaterally suspending enforcement of AI-related regulations, citing legal uncertainty and economic pressure. This de facto fragmentation undermines the credibility of the EU's regulatory framework, prompting private firms to shift compliance planning toward national silos rather than a unified standard.",
